---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="tokiOS — Distributed Agent Operating System"
  description="tokiOS is an experimental Distributed Agent Operating System that provides identity, governed context, persistent state, authority, coordination, and durable execution for multiple AI agents."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Distributed agent systems research</p>

      <h1>An operating system that gives AI agents durable identity, governed context, persistent state, and concurrent execution.</h1>

      <p class="hero-copy">
        Foundation models provide inference. tokiOS provides the systems layer
        around them: identity, governed context, persistent state, authority,
        capabilities, coordination, isolation, recovery, and durable concurrent
        execution across distributed infrastructure.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/research/">Explore the research</a>
        <a
          class="button"
          href="/research/tokimind/governed-persistent-memory-300h/"
        >
          Read the tokiMind study
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-strip" aria-label="Published research evidence">
        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>300 hours</strong>
          <span>Longitudinal evaluation</span>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>1,932 runs</strong>
          <span>Durable scheduled executions</span>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>350 / 350</strong>
          <span>tokiMind scored recall</span>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>Published V1</strong>
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23175185">
            10.5281/zenodo.23175185
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Category definition</p>
      <h2>What is a Distributed Agent Operating System?</h2>

      <p class="lead definition">
        A Distributed Agent Operating System is the systems layer that provides
        and governs identity, context, authority, persistent state, capabilities,
        concurrent execution, coordination, isolation, and recovery for multiple
        AI agents across distributed infrastructure.
      </p>

      <div class="category-grid">
        <article class="category-card">
          <span>Framework</span>
          <p>Helps developers build an agent.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="category-card">
          <span>Harness</span>
          <p>Helps developers test, inspect, simulate, debug, and control agents.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="category-card">
          <span>Runtime / orchestrator</span>
          <p>Executes agents and coordinates units of work.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="category-card category-card-emphasis">
          <span>Distributed Agent Operating System</span>
          <p>
            Governs the ongoing existence and concurrent operation of multiple
            agents across identity, context, state, authority, execution,
            coordination, isolation, and recovery.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section system-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">System layers</p>
      <h2>Governed execution. Governed state. Reproducible evaluation.</h2>

      <p class="lead">
        tokiOS is the broader multi-agent systems layer. VICA governs invocation
        and context, tokiMind governs persistent state, and tokiLab provides the
        experimental infrastructure used to evaluate the system.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>VICA</h3>
          <p>
            Governed invocation and context control across agent identity,
            authority, admissible context, capabilities, tools, policy, and
            model execution.
          </p>
        </article>

        <a
          class="card card-link"
          href="/research/tokimind/governed-persistent-memory-300h/"
        >
          <h3>tokiMind</h3>
          <p>
            Governed persistent state with provenance, authority, contradiction
            handling, supersession, freshness, revocation, and scoped retrieval.
          </p>
          <span class="card-cta">View published research →</span>
        </a>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>tokiLab</h3>
          <p>
            Experimental infrastructure for frozen, durable, longitudinal
            evaluation of agent behavior and state-management systems.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
